// The same defect in LOCAL-declaration position, which looked checked and was not.
//
// A diagnostic did exist here — "cannot bind this to the contract ... it needs a named value, or a
// primitive that declares the conformance" — but it was the fall-through `else` of the emission cascade,
// so it fired only for a value `exprClass` cannot type. That caught a plain enum and missed every CLASS:
// a class took the `isClass(c)` branch above it and emitted `Plain__as_Hashable` for clang to discover
// did not exist. A check that only sees the cases its neighbours could not classify is not a check.
type value Plain { public int32 v = 0; public ctor make() { this.v = 0; } }

fn int32 main()
{
    Plain p = Plain.make();
    Hashable h = p;
    return 0;
}
